==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰerH-|id=pierce}}
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:boryng<t:making a hole>|text=+|tree=1}} {{surf|en|bore|-ing}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɔː.ɹɪŋ/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈboɹ.ɪŋ/|a=GenAm}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-boring.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈboː.ɹɪŋ/|/ˈboɹ.ɪŋ/|a=rhotic,non-horse-hoarse}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈboə.ɹɪŋ/|a=non-rhotic,non-horse-hoarse}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːɹɪŋ|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The act or process of [[bore#Verb|boring]] holes; such practice as an area of expertise in manufacturing.
## {{senseid|en|Q3210331}} {{lb|en|[[machining]]}} Enlarging an existing hole with a single-point cutting tool or a boring head {{n-g|(usually with high precision and accuracy regarding the roundness and size of the hole)}}.
##: {{hyper|en|machining#Noun|cutting#Noun}}
##: {{hypo|en|counterboring#Noun|backboring#Noun}}
##: {{cot|en|boring<id:Q890886><qq:woodworking sense>|reaming#Noun|turning#Noun|milling#Noun|broaching#Noun|shaping#Noun|planing#Noun|grinding#Noun}}
##: {{coi|en|turning and '''boring'''}}
##: {{ux|en|fine '''boring''' with a boring head on a boring mill}}
## {{senseid|en|Q890886}} {{lb|en|especially in [[woodworking]]}} [[drilling#English:_Q890886|Drilling]].
##: {{hyper|en|cutting#Noun}}
##: {{cot|en|boring<id:Q3210331><qq:machining sense>|reaming#Noun|turning#Noun|milling#Noun|planing#Noun|sawing#Noun|whittling#Noun|woodcarving#Noun|sanding#Noun}}
## {{lb|en|AU}} The act of drilling a well into an [[artesian]] basin.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1911|author={{w|Steele Rudd|‘Steel Rudd’}}|title=The Book of Dan|location=Brisbane|publisher=University of Queensland Press|year_published=1970|page=1|passage=And Dan indignantly waved his long, brown arm over the plant, which consisted of the engine, the '''boring''' apparatus, and a dilapidated spring-cartthat was pulled by a lean, lonely-looking horse[.]}}
# A [[pit]] or [[hole]] which has been [[bore#Verb|bore]]d.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1992|author=J. Patrick Powers|title=Construction dewatering: new methods and applications|page=191
|passage=It is common in urban areas that a great many '''borings''' exist from prior construction work.}}
# {{lb|en|usually|in the plural}} One of the [[fragment]]s thrown up when something is bored or drilled.
#: {{syn|en|chip#Noun<alt:chips>|swarf#Noun<qq:wood, metal, or plastic>}}
#: {{hypo|en|shaving#Noun<alt:shavings><qq:wood, plastic>|swarf<qq:metal>}}
#: {{cot|en|shaving#Noun<alt:shavings>|sawdust<qq:wood>}}

